<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="AZD: Work item timeline, children and attachments" id="Azd-Work-Item-Timeline">

    <primary-label ref="azd"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter,procedure" depth="2"/>

    <link-summary>Read a work item's history, comment with mentions and files, see its parent, children, related work, pull requests and branches, and manage its attachments.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Comment on a work item, see its children and linked pull requests, and attach files.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>The AZD work item editor in JetBrains IDEs: timeline and comments with @mentions, child and related work items,
        linked pull requests, commits and branches, and attachments.</web-summary>

    <p>
        Each open work item has an editor tab named <control>Work Item #&lt;id&gt; timeline</control>, with two tabs:
        <control>Timeline</control>, and <control>Children</control> or <control>Related</control>.
        To open it again after you close it, click <control>Timeline ↗</control> at the top of the work item's details tab.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Timeline" id="work-item-timeline">
        <p>
            The <control>Timeline</control> tab shows the comments and the history of the work item.
            Its top row says who last updated the work item and when.
        </p>
        <!-- planned-image src="azd_boards_timeline.png" alt="Work item timeline with the Updated by row, the event filter, comments and the comment box" -->
        <p>
            To show only some events, click the filter at the top right and select one or more of
            <control>Comments</control>, <control>State Changes</control>, <control>Field Changes</control>,
            <control>Link Changes</control> and <control>System Fields</control>.
            Select <control>All Events</control> to show everything again.
        </p>
        <p>
            The top row stays visible while you scroll. To let it scroll away, clear
            <a href="Azd-Settings-Configuration.topic" anchor="ui-customization">Keep the timeline's top row visible while scrolling</a>.
        </p>
        <procedure title="Comment on a work item" id="comment-work-item">
            <step>
                <p>In the <control>Timeline</control> tab, type in the comment box at the bottom.
                    Type <code>@</code> to mention a person.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>Optional: to attach files, click the paperclip icon above the comment box, or paste a screenshot or copied files.
                    AZD uploads each file and inserts a link at the caret. A file that cannot be attached is named under the box with the reason.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>Click <control>Add Comment</control>, or press <shortcut>Ctrl+Enter</shortcut> (macOS: <shortcut>⌘ Enter</shortcut>).</p>
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <procedure title="Edit or delete your comment" id="edit-work-item-comment">
            <p>You can edit and delete only your own comments.</p>
            <step>
                <p>Hover over your comment.
                    A pencil icon and a delete icon appear at the top right of the comment.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>To edit the comment, click the pencil icon, change the text, and click <control>Save Changes</control>
                    or press <shortcut>Ctrl+Enter</shortcut> (macOS: <shortcut>⌘ Enter</shortcut>).
                    Press <shortcut>Esc</shortcut> to cancel.
                    Type <code>@</code> to mention a person.</p>
                <p>If the comment changed after you started editing, click <control>Reload</control> to load the new text,
                    or <control>Overwrite</control> to save yours anyway.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>To delete the comment, click the delete icon, and click <control>Yes</control> in the <control>Delete Comment</control> dialog.</p>
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>
            The IDE edits only comments stored in Markdown on Azure DevOps Services.
            For your other comments, such as older HTML comments and all comments on Azure DevOps Server,
            the pencil icon is disabled; edit them in the browser.
            You can still delete them in the IDE.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Children, related work and development" id="children-tab">
        <p>
            The second tab is <control>Children</control> for work item types that can have children, such as epics, features and stories,
            and <control>Related</control> for the others, such as tasks. The number in the tab name counts the linked items.
        </p>
        <!-- planned-image src="azd_boards_children.png" alt="Children tab with the parent link, Add child, the children tree and the Related Work and Development sections" -->
        <list>
            <li><control>Parent</control> links to the parent work item.</li>
            <li>The children tree lists the child work items. Select <control>Show hierarchy</control> to see their children too,
                and use <control>Expand all</control> and <control>Collapse all</control>.
                Double-click a work item to open it.
                Click <control>Add child</control> to create a child; see <a href="Azd-Create-Work-Item.topic" anchor="add-child"/>.</li>
            <li><control>Related Work</control> lists the other links, such as <control>Related</control>, <control>Predecessor</control>,
                <control>Successor</control> and <control>Duplicate</control>.</li>
            <li><control>Development</control> lists the linked pull requests, commits and branches.
                A pull request of the connected repository opens in the <control>AZD Pull Requests</control> tool window when
                <a href="Azd-Settings-Configuration.topic" anchor="general-configuration">Open AZD links in tool window</a> is selected;
                otherwise, it opens in the browser.
                You can open a link in the browser, copy a commit's SHA or a branch name, and check out a branch that exists in your local repository.</li>
        </list>
        <p>If you can't see some child work items, for example because they are in a project you can't access, the tab says how many are hidden.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Attachments" id="work-item-attachments">
        <p>
            The <control>Attachments</control> section of the <control>Children</control> or <control>Related</control> tab lists the files attached to the work item,
            with their size, date and comment. Switch between <control>List view</control> and <control>Grid view</control> to see rows or thumbnails.
        </p>
        <p>To attach files, do one of the following:</p>
        <list>
            <li>Click <control>Attach Files…</control> and select one or more files.</li>
            <li>Drag files from the <control>Project</control> tool window or from your file manager onto the section.</li>
            <li>Copy a screenshot or files, click the section, and press <shortcut>Ctrl+V</shortcut> (macOS: <shortcut>⌘ V</shortcut>).</li>
        </list>
        <p>
            Each file uploads on its own, and uploads continue when you close the tab.
            While the details tab has unsaved changes, attaching is disabled: click <control>Apply</control> or <control>Revert</control> first.
            Azure DevOps Services accepts files up to 60 MB; Azure DevOps Server allows 4 MB by default, and your administrator can change it.
        </p>
        <p>Right-click an attachment for these actions:</p>
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="Open">Opens an image or a text file of up to 20 MB in an editor tab. Other files open with <control>Save As…</control>.</def>
            <def title="Save As…">Downloads the file to a folder you choose.</def>
            <def title="Open in Browser">Opens the file in your browser.</def>
            <def title="Copy Attachment Link">Copies a download link. Azure DevOps Services only.</def>
            <def title="Edit Comment…">Changes the comment shown under the file name.</def>
            <def title="Remove">Removes the file from the work item. Azure DevOps keeps the file for 28 days, and you can still delete it permanently in that time.</def>
            <def title="Delete Permanently">Deletes the file from Azure DevOps. Every link to it, including images in descriptions and comments, stops working. Azure DevOps Services only.</def>
        </deflist>
        <note title="Delete Permanently needs more access">
            <list>
                <li><b>Sign in with Microsoft:</b> AZD offers to sign in again; select <control>Full access</control>.</li>
                <li><b>Personal access token:</b> add <control>Work Items: Read, write &amp; manage</control> to your token.</li>
                <li>You also need the <control>Permanently delete work items</control> permission in the project.</li>
            </list>
        </note>
        <chapter title="Attachments in remote development" id="attachments-remote-development">
            <p>When AZD runs on a remote development host:</p>
            <list>
                <li><control>Attach Files…</control> and <control>Save As…</control> show the files of the host, not of your computer.</li>
                <li>Dragging files from your computer and pasting copied files are not supported. Paste a screenshot, or copy the file to the host first.</li>
                <li><control>Open with System App</control> is not offered after a download.</li>
                <li><control>Open in Browser</control> works when your browser can reach the Azure DevOps server, for example over the same VPN.</li>
            </list>
        </chapter>
    </chapter>

    <seealso>
        <category ref="related">
